Description: Executes the distributed OHDSI network study pipeline for large-scale
  clinical concept association mining (Concept AB Mining Engine v57). All SQL code was
  written by Stephen H. Bandeian, MD, JD (Principal Investigator, Johns Hopkins University
  School of Medicine). Full credit, scientific authorship, and intellectual attribution
  for all SQL algorithms (init, batch, finalize), database architectures, random
  partitioning logic, healthcare utilization stratification, continuity-corrected
  directionality formulations, and analytical code belong to Dr. Stephen H. Bandeian.
  Computes encounter-level and population-level co-occurrence statistics across OMOP CDM
  standard clinical domains (Condition, Drug, Measurement, Procedure, Device, Observation)
  partitioned into random batches to optimize memory and disk utilization. Evaluates
  temporal precedence, crude and healthcare utilization-stratified lift, odds ratios,
  and continuity-corrected directionality ratios with complete privacy preservation and
  zero patient-level data export.
